    "message": "240 of the 432 channels of the search's TmtDesign.txt have no row of the SDRF naming their file and label, so their assays sit on the design's own sample (its `Sample Name`), with nothing known about it. E.g. `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT126`, `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT127C`, `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT127N` and 429 more."
   },
   {
    "code": "low_core_use",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "10.66 avg cores of 32 allowed (S5)"
   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_uncoded",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The deposited SDRF describes its samples only as text with no ontology term, so the curated organism part, cell type, disease and individual columns are empty. The text is in sample_characteristics: cell type: endothelial cell. Match on it as text; it has not been mapped to a term."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 895 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "unresolved_modifications",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "10 modification(s) could not be mapped to a UNIMOD accession or a mass, and are carried in ProForma as [Info:...] tags: UniProt:(3S)-3-hydroxyasparagine on N, UniProt:(3S)-3-hydroxyaspartate on D, UniProt:(3S)-3-hydroxyhistidine on H, UniProt:3'-nitrotyrosine on Y, UniProt:5-glutamyl serotonin on Q, UniProt:N6-crotonyllysine on K, UniProt:N6-malonyllysine on K, UniProt:N6-succinyllysine on K, UniProt:O-palmitoleoyl serine on S, UniProt:S-(15-deoxy-Delta12,14-prostaglandin J2-9-yl)cysteine on C. Their ptm_sites rows exist and carry modification_name, with modification null, so a query by name finds them and a query by UNIMOD accession will not."
   },
   {
    "code": "isobaric_reference_channels",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "240 channel(s) of the search's TmtDesign.txt are not study samples: `Sample Type` empty: `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT127N`, `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT128N`, `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT129N`, `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT130C`, `PXD077152:20231115_AS_LC4_GT_BG_miP100_WCP_400ng_F01:TMT130N` and 235 more. Their values measure that reference, not a sample of the question. The design is copied in `sources/`."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_ingested",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "PTM site occupancy was not stored: this is a TMT dataset, and MetaMorpheus computes intensity occupancy for label-free searches only; its count occupancy is per file, repeated on every channel (QuantProject DEF-OCC-INT). `ptm_stoichiometry` has no rows here because of that, not because no site was modified."
   }
